wined3d: do not evict the system memory of a texture that has a DC

wined3d_texture_create_dc() makes a DIB section over the texture's system
memory, and the DC keeps using that memory until it is destroyed.
wined3d_texture_evict_sysmem() freed the memory anyway when another
location became valid: after wined3d_swapchain_resize_buffers() it freed
the back buffer's memory under the DC the GDI swapchain had made over it.
After the next swapchain_gdi_present() (which exchanges the front and back
buffers' memory and DCs) the front buffer's DC drew from the freed memory:
Half-Life full screen (DirectDraw on the no-3D adapter) showed vertical
stripes, the DC's bits 0x073e0030 against the texture's 0x0fb10030, and a
read of them faulted.

A texture with a DC keeps its system memory.

--- a/dlls/wined3d/texture.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/texture.c
@@ -119,6 +119,19 @@
     }
 }
 
+/* A DC made by wined3d_texture_create_dc() draws into the system memory it was made over. */
+static bool wined3d_texture_has_dc(const struct wined3d_texture *texture)
+{
+    unsigned int i, sub_count = texture->level_count * texture->layer_count;
+
+    if (!texture->dc_info)
+        return false;
+    for (i = 0; i < sub_count; ++i)
+        if (texture->dc_info[i].dc)
+            return true;
+    return false;
+}
+
 static void wined3d_texture_evict_sysmem(struct wined3d_texture *texture)
 {
     struct wined3d_texture_sub_resource *sub_resource;
@@ -126,7 +139,8 @@
 
     if ((texture->flags & WINED3D_TEXTURE_CONVERTED)
             || texture->resource.pin_sysmem
-            || texture->download_count > WINED3D_TEXTURE_DYNAMIC_MAP_THRESHOLD)
+            || texture->download_count > WINED3D_TEXTURE_DYNAMIC_MAP_THRESHOLD
+            || wined3d_texture_has_dc(texture))
     {
         TRACE("Not evicting system memory for texture %p.\n", texture);
         return;
